2026-11-16 04:11:20,977 INFO deepagent.transcript: [ai] tool_calls=[task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/001-platform-foundation. Feature title: Platform foundation, access control and availability. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: CI/CD, EKS dev/stg/prod envs, External Secrets, Postgres/Redis provisioning, observability/availability monitoring, deploy of api/web/worker, users/boards/board-membership schema, auth, board-member authorisation, Alembic migration setup). Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers requirements: NFR-2 and NFR-3.\n- NFR-2 Availability: 99.5% monthly for the web app and API. Architecture service levels: API latency p95 300ms, error rate 1%, availability 99.5% monthly.\n- NFR-3 Security & privacy: only board members can see a board's tasks; task data is confidential.\nArchitecture: AWS us-east-1, EKS, three environments dev/stg/prod, monthly infra budget USD 2,500 across all envs; target 200 teams, peak 50 req/s. Components ARCH-001 taskflow-api (Python 3.12 FastAPI, repo acme/taskflow-api), ARCH-002 taskflow-web (Node 22 React, acme/taskflow-web, only public entry point), ARCH-003 taskflow-db (PostgreSQL 16), ARCH-004 taskflow-cache (Redis 7), ARCH-005 notify-worker (same repo/image as api, different command). Secrets (DB URL, Redis URL, email provider key) in AWS Secrets Manager via External Secrets; none in Git. Infra repo: acme/taskflow-infra. Team: backend (Alice), frontend (Bob), fullstack (Carol), devops (Dave, 50%). Auth mechanism is not stated: record as assumption + open question. Make user stories for: environments & CI/CD, secrets, users/boards/membership + authentication, board-member authorisation enforced on every board-scoped endpoint, monitoring/alerting for availability and SLOs. Each user story must be sized to at most 13 story points (split bigger ones). Do not invent facts; unknowns become assumptions in spec.md. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' (no extra answers). Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': 'Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/002-tasks-board. Feature title: Tasks and board with live updates. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: task model & CRUD, board columns, SSE + Redis pub/sub board updates, board UI, keyboard accessibility). Foundation (users, boards, membership, auth, authorisation, CI, environments) belongs to feature 001-platform-foundation; reuse, do not recreate. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-1, FR-2, US-1, US-2, NFR-1, NFR-4.\n- US-1 (Must): As a team member, I want to create tasks with a title, description, due date and assignee so that all work is in one place. Given I am on a board, When I create a task with a title, Then it appears in the "To do" column. Given a task, When I set a due date and an assignee, Then both are shown on the task card.\n- US-2 (Must): As a team member, I want to move tasks across the columns To do, Doing and Done so that everyone sees the current state. Given a task in "To do", When I drag it to "Doing", Then all board viewers see it in "Doing" within 5 seconds.\n- FR-1: Users can create, view, edit and delete tasks with title, description, due date and assignee. (US-1)\n- FR-2: Boards have three columns (To do, Doing, Done); users move tasks between them and every viewer sees the change within 5 seconds. (US-2)\n- NFR-1 Performance: board updates visible within 5 seconds (search part belongs to feature 003).\n- NFR-4 Accessibility: board and task forms usable with keyboard only (WCAG 2.1 AA).\nArchitecture: taskflow-api (FastAPI, acme/taskflow-api), taskflow-web (React, acme/taskflow-web), PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7 (caches board reads). Board updates reach other viewers through server-sent events from taskflow-api, backed by Redis pub/sub. API p95 300ms. Pilot beta deadline 2026-12-18 (FR-1, FR-2) so these are top priority. Task assignment must emit an event/hook for feature 005 (assignment email) to consume. Task cards will need story points field? PRD does not say for tasks, but FR-8 burndown needs remaining story points: assume an optional story_points field on task and flag as assumption/open question. Keep each user story to at most 13 story points (split bigger ones, e.g. backend CRUD, board UI, drag-move, live updates SSE, keyboard accessibility). Do not invent facts; unknowns become assumptions. Request history: requests 1-3 all say \'Break prd.md down into a backlog.\' Return a short report of files created.'}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/003-search. Feature title: Full-text task search. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: search endpoint, GIN index/tsvector migration, search cache in Redis). Task model belongs to 002-tasks-board, board membership/auth to 001-platform-foundation; reuse. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-4, US-4.\n- US-4 (Must): As a team member, I want to search tasks so that I can find any task quickly. Given 10,000 tasks, When I search by a word in the title, Then results appear in under 300 ms (p95).\n- FR-4: Full-text search over task titles and descriptions of the user's boards. (US-4)\n- NFR-1: search p95 under 300 ms for 10,000 tasks. NFR-3: only board members see tasks (results limited to the user's boards).\nArchitecture: Search uses PostgreSQL full-text search (GIN index) before considering a separate search engine. Redis 7 caches board reads and search results. taskflow-api FastAPI, taskflow-web React search UI. Include a load/performance test story for the 10,000 task / p95 300 ms target, keyboard-usable search UI (NFR-4). Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts; unknowns (language config, cache TTL) become assumptions. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/004-comments-mentions. Feature title: Comments and @mentions. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: comments and mentions model, mention parsing, feature flag FEATURE_COMMENTS). The notification outbox and email client are owned by 005-assignment-email; reuse them for mention notifications. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-3, US-3.\n- US-3 (Should): As a team member, I want to comment on tasks and mention teammates so that discussions stay with the work. Given a task, When I post a comment mentioning @alice, Then Alice receives a notification.\n- FR-3: Users can comment on tasks and mention teammates with @name; a mention notifies the teammate. (US-3)\n- Assumption from PRD: email is the only notification channel in this release. Mention notifications are subject to preferences (feature 007) when available. NFR-3: only board members can see comments / be mentioned. NFR-4 keyboard usable.\nArchitecture: taskflow-api (FastAPI), taskflow-web (React), PostgreSQL (system of record for comments), notify-worker (ARCH-005, same repo as api) sends emails. Open question for the spec: @name matching rules (username vs display name, non-members) is not defined: record as assumption and open question. Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/005-assignment-email. Feature title: Assignment email notification. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: email provider client, notify-worker skeleton/entrypoint, notification outbox, assignment email). Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-5, US-5 (goal G2: no assigned task is missed; assignees learn within minutes).\n- US-5 (Must): As an assignee, I want an email when a task is assigned to me so that I never miss new work. Given a task, When it is assigned to me, Then I receive one email within 1 minute.\n- FR-5: An email is sent to the assignee within 1 minute of an assignment. (US-5)\n- Assumption from PRD: email is the only notification channel in this release.\nArchitecture: notify-worker (ARCH-005, Python 3.12, same repository acme/taskflow-api and same image as the api, started with a different command; depends on PostgreSQL ARCH-003) sends assignment emails and the daily digest through the email provider's API. Email provider key in AWS Secrets Manager via External Secrets (secrets owner/infra: 001-platform-foundation; the wiring of the key into the worker pod belongs here as a task in acme/taskflow-infra or reference). The provider itself is not named in the architecture: assumption + open question. Task assignment event comes from 002-tasks-board. Requirements: exactly one email per assignment (idempotency, retries), delivery within 1 minute, no email when self-assigned? (not stated: open question), failure handling/observability. Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/006-daily-digest. Feature title: Daily due-tomorrow digest. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: digest scheduler and per-user time zone field; flag FEATURE_DIGEST). Email client and worker skeleton are owned by 005-assignment-email; reuse. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-6, US-6.\n- US-6 (Should): As a team member, I want a daily digest of tasks due tomorrow so that I can plan my day. Given tasks due tomorrow assigned to me, When the daily digest runs at 08:00 in my time zone, Then I receive one email listing them.\n- FR-6: A daily digest email of tasks due tomorrow, sent at 08:00 in the user's time zone.\n- Assumption from PRD: email is the only notification channel. Digest honours preferences from 007 when present.\nArchitecture: notify-worker (ARCH-005, same repo/image as taskflow-api) sends the daily digest through the email provider API; PostgreSQL stores users/tasks. How the worker is scheduled (Kubernetes CronJob vs internal scheduler), how a user's time zone is captured, and whether users with no due tasks get an email (assume no) are not stated: assumptions + open questions. Handle DST, exactly-once per user per day. Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': "Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/007-notification-prefs. Feature title: Notification preferences. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: notification preferences model, API and UI; flag FEATURE_NOTIFICATION_PREFS). Senders (assignment email, digest, mention) are owned by 005/006/004 and must consult preferences. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-7, US-7.\n- US-7 (Could): As a team member, I want to choose which notifications I get and how often, so that I am not overwhelmed.\n- FR-7: Per-user notification preferences: channel and frequency.\n- PRD assumption: email is the only notification channel in this release.\n- PRD OPEN QUESTION (undecided by the client): which channels besides email should FR-7 offer, and which frequencies (immediate, hourly, daily)? Do NOT decide: specify with email as the only channel and keep frequencies as an assumption/open question ([NEEDS CLARIFICATION] handled by assumption), design the data model so channels/frequencies are configurable. Put this open question in the spec so it ends up on the affected stories.\nArchitecture: taskflow-api (FastAPI), taskflow-web (React settings page, keyboard usable NFR-4), PostgreSQL, notify-worker (ARCH-005). Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts. Request history: requests 1-3 all say 'Break prd.md down into a backlog.' Return a short report of files created."}); task({'subagent_type': 'speckit-feature', 'description': 'Project: clinic-test-2 (TaskFlow). feature_directory: specs/008-reports-export. Feature title: Burndown report and CSV export. Create spec.md, plan and tasks.md via spec-kit. Read /outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/implementation-contract.md and follow it (this feature OWNS: sprint model, burndown report, CSV export; flags FEATURE_BURNDOWN, FEATURE_CSV_EXPORT). Task model is from 002-tasks-board; auth/membership from 001. Also read /outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md and architecture.md.\nCovers: FR-8, FR-9, US-8, US-9 (goal G3: managers can answer \'are we on track?\' without a status meeting).\n- US-8 (Should): As a manager, I want a burndown chart per board so that I can see whether we will finish on time. Given a board with a sprint, When I open the report, Then I see remaining points per day for the sprint.\n- US-9 (Could): As a manager, I want to export board data as CSV so that I can analyse it elsewhere. Given a board, When I click Export, Then I download a CSV with one row per task and all task fields.\n- FR-8: Burndown chart per board showing remaining story points per day of the current sprint. (US-8)\n- FR-9: CSV export of a board: one row per task with all task fields. (US-9)\n- PRD OPEN QUESTION: is "Done" the only column that counts toward the burndown? Do not decide; assume Done only, record as assumption and open question on the burndown story. Also not defined: how sprints are created/managed on a board (assume a minimal sprint entity with start/end dates, a manager sets it) and where story points live on tasks (assume an optional story_points field added by 002-tasks-board). Manager role is not otherwise defined in the architecture: assumption. Daily snapshot approach for remaining points per day is a design choice for the plan. NFR-3 only board members; CSV must not leak data across boards; guard against CSV injection (assumption). Architecture: taskflow-api (FastAPI, reports and CSV export), taskflow-web (React chart, keyboard accessible), PostgreSQL. Keep each user story at most 13 points. Do not invent facts. Request history: requests 1-3 all say \'Break prd.md down into a backlog.\' Return a short report of files created.'})] 
